For fighter classes like Valk, a helm of brilliance can mean the
difference between being able to cast a spell, and not.
Definitely worth a wish, IMHO.  (Telepathy is very useful as
well, but just putting on a blindfold or a towel from time to
time is usually sufficient.)

> Slow
> digestion becomes less useful after you get all the food
> rations from the castle soldiers, but it's nice for the
> midgame and Famine.

I find it mainly useful for spellcaster types in the early game.
When you're using nutrition too fast to be able to pray each
time you become weak.  Otherwise, I don't think I've ever
bothered.  (I might if I had four or five ring fingers.  But in
a lot of games, there are at least three other rings that I want
to wear all of the time.)

> I'd also add some miscellaneous items:
> blessed unicorn horn

Essential.

> blessed luckstone

I've found that it's not generally necessary to have it blessed.
(But of course, later on, you've generally got so much holy
water that you don't know what to do with it, and blessing it
doesn't hurt.)

